OneTimeUseIdPolicy::check1271SignedAction
├── given the configId was never initialized
│   └── it should return false
├── given the caller is the executor
│   └── it should return false, burned or not, nominated or not
├── given the caller is neither Permit2 nor the executor (e.g. the Compact route)
│   └── it should fail closed and return false even with a matching nomination
├── given the caller is Permit2 (the settling check)
│   ├── given the signature is shorter than the nonce field
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given the executor has not consumed the presented nonce
│   │   └── it should return false even with a matching nomination
│   ├── given this transaction validated a consumeFor naming the presented nonce
│   │   └── it should return true
│   ├── given this transaction validated a consumeFor naming a DIFFERENT nonce
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given this transaction validated only a consume
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given no burn was validated
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given a second settlement presents its own nonce after the first already settled
│   │   └── it should return false (and its own burn is refused at validation)
│   ├── given the nomination was recorded under another multiplexer
│   │   └── it should return false
│   ├── given the witness is Permit2 nonce zero
│   │   └── it should still settle
│   ├── given the witness is the max uint256 nonce
│   │   └── it should still settle
│   └── given the burn happened in an earlier transaction
│       └── it should return false
└── given a deadline is pinned
    ├── when the deadline is in the future
    │   └── it should settle on a proven burn
    ├── when the current timestamp equals the deadline
    │   └── it should settle (inclusive)
    ├── when the deadline has passed
    │   └── it should refuse even a correctly proven burn
    └── when the deadline is zero
        └── it should settle long after install
